+ * Memory for CONNSYS, outside XNU's (above): its "EMI" (the firmware's images, logs, dumps),
+ * 1 MB-aligned in Android's 0x50000000..0x8fffffff, Android's size rounded up; and Wi-Fi's DMA
+ * memory (rings and buffers), 16 MB-aligned as Android's wifi-reserve-memory. Both clear of
+ * what LK loads there: the recovery image's ramdisk (TWRP's, ~36 MB) at 0x51100000, unused
+ * once XNU runs but kept out of the way all the same.
